  "description": "Bean qou-wapd. Computes tr_M(beta_EW Delta_I) at N=3, where the lambda=(3,2,1) block is OCCUPIED (l(lambda)=3 <= N) and its Ocneanu weight is nonzero -- as against N=2, where the Schur-Weyl row cap sends it to zero and the corpus's appendix-standard-model ruling places every route from the block outside the carrier. The corpus separately holds that the flavour sector requires N=3, that the mass channel cannot be retuned to it, and therefore that a SECOND Markov trace on the same H_n(q) is needed -- already typeable, since HnMarkovTrace.lean carries the Markov parameter as a free class field. This probe asks the resulting empirical question: what is the N=3 trace of this word, and does it approach cot(theta_W)? It does NOT claim N=3 is the right reading of the EW sector; the corpus's preferred lever is the Milnor triple linking, and the coupling normalisation is open.",
